  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday) \nIssued at 1223 AM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nOn Monday, scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms will\ncontinue over east central and southeast areas, where moist \nsoutheast low-level return flow will continue as a weak trailing \ndisturbance crosses aloft. PWATs are forecast to trend downward, \nso the risk of additional flash flooding will be low on Monday. \nOtherwise, drier and warmer weather is forecast Monday through \nmidweek as an active storm track north of NM draws dry west and \nsouthwest flow over the forecast area. High temperatures will \nclimb near 1991-2020 averages areawide starting Tuesday, then as \nmuch as 8 degrees above the averages on the eastern plains \nWednesday. Models have come into better agreement on an upper \nlevel low pressure system dropping southward along the Pacific NW \ncoast during the latter half of the week. This system will draw a \nrich return flow of Gulf moisture into the forecast area starting \nWednesday night with increasing coverage of showers and \nthunderstorms over southern areas Thursday. Showers and storms \nwill increase in coverage areawide Friday and Friday night as a \nshort-wave trough crosses NM from the southwest.",
